<title>GREECE: Greece lifts remaining foreign exchange controls.</title>
<headline>Greece lifts remaining foreign exchange controls.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Greece moved to lift remaining foreign exchange controls on Tuesday, saying Greek residents and legal entities would be allowed to hold foreign exchange deposits with local credit institutions effective August 1.</p>
<p>&quot;Greek residents, individuals and legal entities, will be allowed to hold deposits in foreign currency without limitations with credit institutions operating in Greece effective August 1 1997,&quot; the central bank said.</p>
</text>
